    "author": "John Keller",
    "description": "Reproduction study — inspired by Express Stave: Pianoforte Notation (John Keller, 2010). Tritone 2-line staff at D/G#; inverse-7-5 fill — the seven naturals solid, the five black-key notes hollow (per the operator reference). B and F sit midway touching neither line (spaces, no config element). Keller's custom D clef (E1) is exercised in register-label (text) mode showing 'D'; the published clef glyph and the piano-symbol line identifier are deferred as assets. DEVIATION (rendering model): the operator reference annotates the Express Stave ledger rule as '(non-repeating staves)' — the published staff is a bounded single octave with the tritone-distant D drawn as a ledger, which the platform's per-octave-repeating staff cannot express (invariant I4). The platform renders its native continuous [2,8] grid where D and G# are staff lines every octave (same line pitch classes), so no D ledger is drawn — recorded, not reproduced. Half/whole-note side strokes (duration 'other', notehead-baked) are not in this single-duration preview. Built from the public gallery description/image; not endorsed by or derived from the original.",
